      "writtenOn": "2024-12-16T18:18:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does that mean the API should be piped threw the companion device manager ?\n\nTo prevent any wrong usage of it ? @okamil@google.com ?",
      "parentUuid": "d9878ec8_79d799c1",
      "revId": "7d33433a56fb151f726b2ad7b0fcd6d1b57ba29d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6f971ec_a51a169d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T00:10:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "companion device manager can be a better approach\n\nbut the main worry is different Apps will be calling this API at unexpected times. \n\nsince the LE ACL connection is a shared resource, allowing all apps to modify a LE connection can lead to bad user experience.",
      "parentUuid": "cb1d28d1_fec2ce18",
      "revId": "7d33433a56fb151f726b2ad7b0fcd6d1b57ba29d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9aa45210_9db5977f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059936
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T00:16:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could see wanting a new, higher-privilege permission related to device management, but it would be quite odd to place the API direclty in CDM.\n\nThat said, I don\u0027t see how this is different from any of the other existing APIs that applications could already call.  It would make more sense to separately introduce a new permission and then apply that to all existing APIs which fall into this category.",
      "parentUuid": "f6f971ec_a51a169d",
      "revId": "7d33433a56fb151f726b2ad7b0fcd6d1b57ba29d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44eb2265_b9487b12",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T00:18:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We already regret having previous APIs that allow such low layer modifications and they ended up leading to sub-optimal behaviors. For example, we used to allow all apps to modify ATT MTU and it led to significant race conditions. \n\nWe had to do an App compat change in 2023 to finally address this and we hoped that we never opened that `configureMtu()` API up. \n\nSee: https://developer.android.com/about/versions/14/behavior-changes-all#mtu-set-to-517",
      "parentUuid": "9aa45210_9db5977f",
      "revId": "7d33433a56fb151f726b2ad7b0fcd6d1b57ba29d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "babc63c2_6f884b87",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T17:51:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So ideally, this should be a public API but guarded by CDM so it can only be called by the companion app related to this LE connection. I agree with Jack that this cannot be just a public API right now, as it could indeed allow apps to interfere with existing LE connections.\n\nAs we\u0027re already past deadlines for 25Q2, I would recommend having this as a SystemApi first and work on a follow up in CDM later for 25Q4.",
      "parentUuid": "44eb2265_b9487b12",
      "revId": "7d33433a56fb151f726b2ad7b0fcd6d1b57ba29d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
